## Cover Letter

Dear Hiring Team,

I'm applying for the Technical Artist role at SuperPlay.

My work has consistently sat at the intersection of art, engine, and tooling — which is exactly the bridge this role asks for. I have around two years of Unity/C# development experience, shader work in HLSL and URP, and a strong pipeline-tooling background: at Wargaming, BLACKHUB Games, and AvaCapo, I built Python-based tools and plugin systems aimed at cutting manual work, catching errors before they hit a build, and speeding up asset delivery. At ChillBase, I worked mobile production specifically — validating incoming assets and troubleshooting engine integration under mobile constraints. At Immerse Lab, I handled rigging, animation setup, import/export pipelines, and shipped VR/XR features in Unity, while also owning documentation and onboarding for the art pipeline.

I don't have hands-on Spine experience, and my VFX/physics-simulation work has been lighter than the shader and rigging side — worth flagging directly rather than glossing over. What I do bring solidly is the GPU optimization, tool-building, and cross-discipline collaboration this role centers on, plus real production experience shipping under performance and memory constraints.

My portfolio is at agamurian.com if you'd like to see examples of the tooling and shader work directly.

Best regards,
Andrey Golovin
